  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197354",
      "title": "Working With Core Components",
      "lectureOrder": 14,
      "videoOrder": 12,
      "sourceHash": "3a4cdd10652c8d5a044775e4402a2ee6c5aefd69d5fa200349dab9d4098e51e5",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 3.72,
          "en": "So let's start by diving deeper",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.72,
          "end": 6.453,
          "en": "into core components like Text and View.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.43,
          "end": 11.43,
          "en": "And for this I'll actually delete this status bar component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.43,
          "end": 12.823,
          "en": "and also this import.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 18.16,
          "en": "If I save that, this is updated here on those devices",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.16,
          "end": 21.963,
          "en": "and not much change here, so we don't need this right now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.4,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "I also will delete this Text component and save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 30.253,
          "en": "so that for now we have a blank screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 31.4,
          "end": 34.517,
          "en": "And now let's try re adding the text like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 34.517,
          "end": 36.67,
          "en": "\"Hello World\" between the View,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 36.67,
          "end": 38.823,
          "en": "without the surrounding text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 40.07,
          "end": 44.223,
          "en": "If we do that, we notice that we get an error down here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 45.06,
          "end": 46.167,
          "en": "We get an error that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.167,
          "end": 49.943,
          "en": "\"Text strengths must be rendered within a Text component\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.78,
          "end": 54.2,
          "en": "which is actually a quite helpful error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 54.2,
          "end": 58.31,
          "en": "which tells us in a pretty clear way, what's wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 58.31,
          "end": 59.92,
          "en": "And before we fix this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 59.92,
          "end": 62.02,
          "en": "let's also take a look at those devices,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.02,
          "end": 63.66,
          "en": "those simulators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.66,
          "end": 66.303,
          "en": "and here we also get the same error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.42,
          "end": 69.78,
          "en": "And this is actually something important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 69.78,
          "end": 71.75,
          "en": "which is why I'm showing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 71.75,
          "end": 73.97,
          "en": "It's different than what you might know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 73.97,
          "end": 75.75,
          "en": "from web development.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 77.95,
          "en": "If you would build a web app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 77.95,
          "end": 80.35,
          "en": "and this would be react for the web",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 80.35,
          "end": 83.61,
          "en": "and this would maybe be a div instead of a View,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 83.61,
          "end": 85.77,
          "en": "then this kind of code would be fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 85.77,
          "end": 88.60300000000001,
          "en": "We could put text inside of a div there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 89.82,
          "end": 94.27000000000001,
          "en": "React Native and native platforms to be precise",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.27000000000001,
          "end": 96.75999999999999,
          "en": "are stricter than that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.75999999999999,
          "end": 100.2,
          "en": "You can't put a Text into a View",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.2,
          "end": 104.08,
          "en": "which is pretty much the equivalent to a div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.08,
          "end": 105.85300000000001,
          "en": "because it's not meant for that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 106.84,
          "end": 111.84,
          "en": "Instead Views, so the of to divs in the web world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.85,
          "end": 116.14,
          "en": "Views are meant to generally build boxes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.14,
          "end": 120.69,
          "en": "and containers that hold other content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.69,
          "end": 125.43,
          "en": "A View could hold some text wrapped into a Text component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 125.43,
          "end": 128.5,
          "en": "It could also hold a TextInput or a button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 128.5,
          "end": 131.153,
          "en": "or an image, or anything like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 132.04,
          "end": 134.89,
          "en": "but you have to put the content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 134.89,
          "end": 139.01,
          "en": "into an element that is able to display it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 139.01,
          "end": 142.66,
          "en": "And the View is only able to hold other components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 142.66,
          "end": 145.05,
          "en": "It's not able to display text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 145.05,
          "end": 148.92000000000002,
          "en": "and that is something really important to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 148.92000000000002,
          "end": 151.8,
          "en": "If you wanna display a text, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 151.8,
          "end": 154.35,
          "en": "you have to use this Text component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 154.35,
          "end": 159.35,
          "en": "and wrap the text opening and closing text around your text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 159.39,
          "end": 162.81,
          "en": "And if you do this and save, then this updates",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 162.81,
          "end": 167.73,
          "en": "and works again, but that's a first important takeaway",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 167.73,
          "end": 172.73,
          "en": "even though we can kind of compare those component to HTML.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 172.98,
          "end": 175.46,
          "en": "And even though it looks kind of similar,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 175.46,
          "end": 178.35,
          "en": "there are important differences.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 178.35,
          "end": 181.64,
          "en": "Now, what you will often do when building React Native apps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 181.64,
          "end": 184.96,
          "en": "is you will build more complex user interfaces",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 184.96,
          "end": 188.64,
          "en": "that don't just have one piece of text inside of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 188.64,
          "end": 190.94,
          "en": "And what's important to understand then",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 190.94,
          "end": 193.53,
          "en": "is that those different core components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 193.53,
          "end": 195.113,
          "en": "have different roles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 196.16,
          "end": 199.63,
          "en": "The Text is a component that's used for, guess what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 199.63,
          "end": 200.993,
          "en": "Displaying text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 202.01,
          "end": 205.37,
          "en": "The View is a component that's meant to hold",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 205.37,
          "end": 209.24,
          "en": "and lay out other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 209.24,
          "end": 211.64,
          "en": "Now, we will learn more about laying things out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 211.64,
          "end": 214.18,
          "en": "with help of styling in a couple of minutes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 214.18,
          "end": 216.36,
          "en": "but the idea behind the View component is that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 216.36,
          "end": 219.57999999999998,
          "en": "you typically have multiple child components in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 219.57999999999998,
          "end": 222.05700000000002,
          "en": "For example, another text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 222.05700000000002,
          "end": 225.107,
          "en": "\"Another piece of text\".",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 226.26,
          "end": 228.34,
          "en": "In a Text component, as you learned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 228.34,
          "end": 230.34,
          "en": "but now we got two of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.34,
          "end": 232.44,
          "en": "And we grouped them together in a View",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.44,
          "end": 235.06,
          "en": "just as we might group them together in a div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 235.06,
          "end": 236.513,
          "en": "if this would be for the web.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 237.5,
          "end": 241.21,
          "en": "Now, in the web, we also have other components like section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 241.21,
          "end": 244.94,
          "en": "or article, here in React Native world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.94,
          "end": 246.69,
          "en": "it's just the View.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.69,
          "end": 249.01,
          "en": "This is our container component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 249.01,
          "end": 252.01,
          "en": "that we use for holding our components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 252.01,
          "end": 255.35,
          "en": "And of course, those other components also can be nested.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 255.35,
          "end": 256.89,
          "en": "We could have another View",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 256.89,
          "end": 260.28,
          "en": "which actually holds this inner text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 260.28,
          "end": 262.74,
          "en": "So this is all something that's totally fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.74,
          "end": 264.793,
          "en": "something you will typically build when building",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 264.793,
          "end": 268.853,
          "en": "more complex user interfaces with React Native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 269.7,
          "end": 273.31,
          "en": "The View then makes it very easy to use styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 273.31,
          "end": 276.1,
          "en": "into which we'll dive in a second to control",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 276.1,
          "end": 279.913,
          "en": "where which of its child elements should be positioned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 280.89,
          "end": 284.95,
          "en": "Of course, we don't just have a View and Text to though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 284.95,
          "end": 287.53,
          "en": "If you take a look at the official website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 287.53,
          "end": 290.38,
          "en": "the official React Native documentation site",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 290.38,
          "end": 292.12,
          "en": "you'll learn that there are more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 292.12,
          "end": 294.11,
          "en": "React Native core components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.11,
          "end": 297.29,
          "en": "and those components fulfill different purposes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 297.29,
          "end": 300.69,
          "en": "We got View and Text, which are two of the most important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 300.69,
          "end": 302.7,
          "en": "and commonly used components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 302.7,
          "end": 306.27,
          "en": "but we also could display a image, add some scrolling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 306.27,
          "end": 308.21,
          "en": "something will do later as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 308.21,
          "end": 313.05,
          "en": "or add a TextInput which allows users to enter some text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 313.05,
          "end": 315.053,
          "en": "We could also add a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 316.38,
          "end": 318.52,
          "en": "and indeed, that is what I'll do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 318.52,
          "end": 321.95,
          "en": "Below this text, I'll add a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.95,
          "end": 324.65,
          "en": "but for this, we need to import it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 324.65,
          "end": 326.3,
          "en": "And that is also important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 326.3,
          "end": 330.63,
          "en": "and an important difference compared to react for the web.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330.63,
          "end": 334.05,
          "en": "With react for the web, you don't need to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 334.05,
          "end": 336.64,
          "en": "the HTL elements you might be using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336.64,
          "end": 338.52,
          "en": "with React Native, you do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 338.52,
          "end": 340.32,
          "en": "If you wanna display a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 340.32,
          "end": 344.27,
          "en": "you have to import this core component from React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 344.27,
          "end": 345.92,
          "en": "and then you can add your button.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 346.83,
          "end": 350.15,
          "en": "And number important difference is that unlike for the web,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 350.15,
          "end": 352.85,
          "en": "you don't build a button like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 352.85,
          "end": 356.35,
          "en": "by adding the caption between the opening and closing tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 356.35,
          "end": 358.89,
          "en": "Instead, it's a self-closing element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 358.89,
          "end": 361.44,
          "en": "where you add a title prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 361.44,
          "end": 364.063,
          "en": "and then you add your title here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 365.96,
          "end": 368.57,
          "en": "This would now display a button as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 368.57,
          "end": 370.44,
          "en": "with the kind of default styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 370.44,
          "end": 373.21,
          "en": "and tap effects you would expect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 373.21,
          "end": 375.35,
          "en": "for the different platforms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 375.35,
          "end": 377.35,
          "en": "And you see that the look adjusts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 377.35,
          "end": 379.11,
          "en": "to the underlying platform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 379.11,
          "end": 381.41,
          "en": "It looks like an iOS button on iOS,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 381.41,
          "end": 383.61,
          "en": "and like an Android button on Android.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 383.61,
          "end": 386,
          "en": "But of course the button doesn't do anything yet",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 386,
          "end": 388.64,
          "en": "because I have added any listener.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 388.64,
          "end": 390.71,
          "en": "Now, we will add interactivity,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 390.71,
          "end": 392.87,
          "en": "and learn how that works later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 392.87,
          "end": 395.21,
          "en": "For the moment, let's just add the button here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 395.21,
          "end": 398.24,
          "en": "and let's understand that we always work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 398.24,
          "end": 400.13,
          "en": "with core components like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 400.13,
          "end": 404.63,
          "en": "where every component has its clearly defined purpose,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 404.63,
          "end": 409.4,
          "en": "and you build your overall UI by combining those components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
